Bun 1.3.3
---------

`bin/jig` is produced by `bun build --compile` using Bun 1.3.3 build
`274e01c7` and contains a copy of that runtime. Bun's exact release license
inventory is:

https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/bun-v1.3.3/LICENSE.md

That inventory says Bun itself is MIT-licensed, lists its embedded and linked
third-party works, and states that JavaScriptCore and WebKit are statically
linked under LGPL-2. It also states that static linking requires application
object form sufficient for a recipient to modify the library and relink the
application.

PUBLICATION BLOCKER: the current Jig package does not contain a pinned complete
license bundle for the Bun runtime and its linked works, or the relinkable
materials required by the LGPL static-link condition described by Bun. The
compiled executable must not be published until those requirements have an
exact, reviewed, reproducible solution. This notice alone is not that solution.

